<p class="climate-footnote">Source: <a href={climateSource}>JMA 1991–2020 normals</a>. A wet day has daily precipitation ≥1 mm, including melted snow; it need not rain all day. Trip estimate = monthly wet days ÷ days in month × trip length, rounded to one decimal. This is a 30-year climate average, <strong>not a forecast or a promise of wet days on your trip</strong>.</p>
